.SH "NAME"
pcre2_jit_stack_free \- free a JIT matching stack
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.ss \n[.ss]
.nf
.fam C
\fB\&#include\fP \fB<pcre2.h>\fP

\fBvoid\fP pcre2_jit_stack_free(\fBpcre2_jit_stack\fP *\fIjit_stack\fP);
.fam
.fi
.ss \n[.ss] 0
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
This function is used to free a JIT stack that was created by
pcre2_jit_stack_create() when it is no longer needed. If the argument is
\fBNULL\fP, the function returns immediately without doing anything. For more
details, see the
\f(CRpcre2jit\fP
page.
.sp
There is a complete description of the PCRE2 native API in the
\f(CRpcre2api\fP
page and a description of the POSIX API in the
\f(CRpcre2posix\fP
page.